# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PortalVault .gitignore
#
# Security rule: secrets and internal legacy data must never reach this
# repository. Rationale and full list: docs/SECURITY.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# .env* is never committed. Only exception: .env.example with placeholders.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Internal legacy data -------------------------------------------------
# These patterns are an extra brake, not a permission: the legacy project
# ../webpage is never copied into this repository in the first place.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
**/inventory.json
**/id_ledger.json
**/ebay.json
**/mappings/
images/master/
data/internal/

# --- Dependencies ---------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# --- Next.js / build ------------------------------------------------------
/.next/
/out/
/build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# --- Tests ----------------------------------------------------------------
/coverage

# --- Logs -----------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Deployment / tooling -------------------------------------------------
.vercel

# --- Editor artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# nano writes <file>.save when an edit is aborted. Such a copy next to a
# migration is dangerous: it is a second, outdated version of a file that is
# meant to be executed exactly once.
*.save
*.swp
*~

# --- OS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Source artwork. The shipped derivatives live in public/images/brand/ and are
# committed; the multi-megabyte originals are kept out of the repository.
/artwork/
